# iDetrend TODO

## Chronology and tree choices are not kept

The kind of chronology, the mean, and how trees are read from the names
are choices on the Results panel. The report records them, but the copy
kept in the browser and the settings file do not, so a restored session
starts with the standard chronology and trees worked out from the names.
The same goes for settings pinned for comparison: they last for the
session only.

## Statistics on large files

Above 120 series the statistics are computed on request, because summary()
of the indices takes time that grows with the square of the number of
series. dplR 1.8.1 makes interseries.cor() several times faster; rwi.stats()
is then the slow part. Raise the limit when the app moves to 1.8.1.

## Gaps

Every gap in a file is filled the same way. dplR 1.8.1's fill.internal.NA()
takes `series`, so gaps could be filled series by series, and it adds
fill = "Chron". Both need 1.8.1.

## Report size

A plot of every series adds about 100 KB a series to the report as drawn
on a Mac (less with the cairo device a Linux server uses). Check the size
on the server for a 200-series file.

## Weights for Friedman's smoother

detrend.series() takes case weights (`wt`) for method "Friedman". The app
does not offer them.
